Full suite `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_*.py'` ran 496 tests, all OK, before the parallel YouTube lane added tests/test_ux_youtube.py. The final run has 516 tests and 3 failures. All three are in test_ux_youtube.py (RouteTableTests, for example test_a_fixture_route_table_points_the_adapter_at_a_fake_api). That lane was still mid-implementation (the file changed at 08:10), and no test reads my three files. `python3 skills/remorsearch-ux-qa/scripts/smoke_loop.py` exits 0. git status shows no stray run folders or page text.

I also ran a scratch validator, /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ux-research-qa-skills/e780fd74-671a-5856-a21d-1181ebfa73fb/scratchpad/kp1/validate.py, which mirrors the planned tests/test_korean_pack.py. It reports 0 errors against the current routes.json (version 2026-09-30.1). It checks that:
- every JSON host is covered by routes.json platforms, out_of_scope or terms_restricted under verdict.host_matches;
- each row's terms.status and terms.routes_entry equal the routes.json terms_restricted entry that covers its hosts, found with scope.terms_entry (rows with no covering entry are unchecked);
- route values are in the vocabulary and none is researcher_note;
- every route_id exists in routes.json;
- the markdown has the same 27 ids in the same order, in both the table and the section headings;
- the markdown URL set equals the URL set of the whole JSON (124 URLs);
- every backticked skill path in both markdown files resolves;
- neither file contains 여성시대, researcher_note, 이용자, 유저, similarweb or img.theqoo, and neither mentions K-skill or insane-*.

Both outputs are generated from one source: scratchpad/kp1/build.py writes the JSON and scratchpad/kp1/md.py writes platform-map.md. I wrote overview.md by hand.

content:platform-map.interface_notes:
korea-platforms.json (schema_version ux-research-korea-platforms.v1, version 2026-09-29.1, checked_at 2026-09-29, verified_at null)

Top-level keys: schema_version, version, checked_at, verified_at, note, vocab, labels, corpus_norms, platforms.
- vocab.route: official_api_user_key | official_feed | team_export | reader_public_page | signed_in_authorised | none. Where "none" appears it is the only route.
- vocab.terms_status: reported | confirmed | checked_by_user | unchecked.
- vocab.terms_restricts: automated_collection | bulk_collection | ai_input | storage (the same as scope.RESTRICTS).
- vocab.stop_class: the same as verdict.STOP_CLASSES.
- vocab.robots_expectation: unknown | reported_closed | not_reached.
- vocab.read_via: direct_fetch | search_index | search_summary | third_party_quote | mirror | not_found | inference | skill_rule.
- vocab.family: blog | community | qna | video | app_store_reviews | microblog | commerce_reviews.
- vocab.public_scope: public | mixed | app_heavy | app_only | private.
- labels maps read_via to the pack's Korean labels: direct_fetch = 관찰됨; search_index, search_summary and third_party_quote = 미확인(요약); mirror = 미확인(미러); not_found = 미확인; inference = 추론; skill_rule = 규칙.

Each platform row has:
- id, name_ko, hosts, route_ids (routes.json platform ids), family, public_scope;
- scope_note {text, read_via, sources, rule_ref?};
- routes (in order of preference), route_notes[], expected_stops[];
- robots {expectation, text, read_via, sources, rule_ref?};
- terms {status, routes_entry, restricts, terms_url, clause, read_via, sources, note, rule_ref?}, where routes_entry is the id of the routes.json terms_restricted entry that covers the row's hosts, or null;
- audience {text, confidence, read_via, sources};
- voice_notes[], privacy_notes[], discontinuities[{date, what, read_via, sources}];
- checked_at, verified_at.

corpus_norms is a list of {id, text, read_via, sources, rule_ref?, legal_ref?}. Its ids are: sensitive-data, hate-speech-corpus, no-community-placement, uncertain-polarity, narrative_unverified, register-not-demographics, anonymous-threads, vote-selection, promotion-first, minors, norms-not-traits. Any URL test must walk the whole JSON, corpus_norms included, not only platforms.

The 27 row ids, in order: naver-blog, naver-cafe, naver-kin, naver-place, kakao-map, daum-cafe, tistory, dcinside, fmkorea, theqoo, nate-pann, clien, ppomppu, ruliweb, instiz, blind, everytime, band, kakaotalk-openchat, daangn, youtube, instagram, threads, app-store-kr (route id app-store), google-play-kr (route id google-play), coupang, delivery-apps (no hosts).

Terms statuses (they agree with routes.json):
- reported: naver-blog, naver-kin and naver-place (entry naver-terms); naver-cafe (naver-cafe-bulk-notice); dcinside (dcinside-terms); coupang (coupang-terms).
- confirmed: youtube (youtube-terms), instagram (meta-instagram), threads (meta-threads).
- All other rows are unchecked.

youtube hosts include youtu.be. threads hosts are threads.com, www.threads.com, threads.net and www.threads.net. ruliweb hosts are bbs.ruliweb.com and m.ruliweb.com.

platform-map.md section numbers (sibling files already cite §4, §7, §8 and §11):
1. 이 지도의 성격, with the label and value legends;
2. 한눈에 보기 (table);
3. 채널별 상세 (### `id` headings);
4. 커뮤니티 콘텐츠 규범(코퍼스 수준), rendered from corpus_norms;
5. 공개 웹에서 덜 잡히는 사용자;
6. 스토어·리뷰 편향;
7. 불연속 날짜표;
8. 행을 고치는 방법 (routes.json first, then the JSON, then this file);
9. Done when;
10. Failure modes;
11. 출처, a keyed list P01-P124 identical to the JSON URL set.
No URL appears before §11.

overview.md section numbers: 1 언제 쓰는가; 2 단계별로 달라지는 점 (A0, A1, A2-A3, A4-A5, A6); 3 한국 실무에서 이 팩이 돕는 방식 (says "public boards only"); 4 요청 강도 신호어 (간단히 wins); 5 하지 않는 일; 6 Done when; 7 Failure modes; 8 이 폴더의 파일.

Code names these files describe, taken from the code as it is now:
- stop class terms_restricted; search pages refused with exit 2 by read, robots and ingest, and a stop when reached through a redirect; switched-off discovery endpoints refused with exit 2; `robots` exits 3 for a terms_restricted host;
- brief access_policy.terms_checked {host, terms_url, checked_on, result: permits_this_reading | restricts_this_reading | unclear, note?}, at most 20 items; a lifted host's budget is 10 documents;
- ethics_review {status: none | exempt | approved | pending, body?, reference?};
- robots reason robots:ai_agent:<token> and the signal ai_training_disallow; uxresearch/data/agent-tokens.json;
- YouTube: env REMORSEARCH_YOUTUBE_API_KEY with alias YOUTUBE_API_KEY; official_route_needs_key; a failed official route ends as terms_restricted; comments_disabled maps to gone; retention_until is the fetch time plus 30 days;
- marker families in markers.json: promotion, promotion_patterns, promotion_placed, promotion_labels, incentive (seller_event, seller_notice, platform_points, reward_unspecified), virtual_person, membership, age_identity, anonymous_handles;
- author-key refuses anonymous handles and handles with a partial IP, and points to --thread-url;
- lexicon.json in the run folder; planned commands merge, gate and report-check.

